WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.890
Leave an iron nail out in the damp,
and before long it's covered in rust.

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.110
Iron atoms are combining with
oxygen to form iron oxide.

3
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:10.830
Electrons are on the move.

4
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.590
But which way do they go?

5
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.330
When iron rusts, does it
gain electrons, or lose them?

6
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:20.470
In this mission, you'll meet four
ways to spot oxidation and reduction,

7
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.270
and assign oxidation states
using a few simple rules.

8
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.710
You'll name oxidizing and reducing agents,

9
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.270
and write and balance
half-equations, even in acid.

10
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:35.240
Your mission: decide whether iron
gains or loses electrons as it rusts.
